1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,130
Save only inside your approved
training environment, then open

2
00:00:04,130 --> 00:00:07,420
the resulting call and confirm
its recipients and alarm level.

3
00:00:07,849 --> 00:00:11,409
A saved call does not establish
that a member received an alert;

4
00:00:11,829 --> 00:00:15,050
verify that separately through
a controlled communication test.

5
00:00:15,470 --> 00:00:18,840
Further alarm levels add
requirements to an active response.

6
00:00:19,209 --> 00:00:22,069
Review those levels before
using Strike Next Alarm.

7
00:00:22,279 --> 00:00:26,059
When starting from a gallery template,
inspect its department mappings,

8
00:00:26,290 --> 00:00:30,040
keep the created card disabled,
and repeat the same saved-plan

9
00:00:30,040 --> 00:00:31,979
test before putting it into use.

10
00:00:32,519 --> 00:00:35,279
The same planning controls
fit other organizations.

11
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:38,770
A community paramedicine or
mental health team can request

12
00:00:38,770 --> 00:00:40,449
a clinician and peer responder.

13
00:00:40,830 --> 00:00:43,770
Search and rescue can request
a search team and leader.

14
00:00:43,970 --> 00:00:47,469
Security can combine a patrol
unit with a site supervisor.

15
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:51,849
Wildland contractors can plan crew
and support resources, while an

16
00:00:51,849 --> 00:00:56,029
